course: dictionary
lesson: 1185
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Just browsing» in a shop and «browse the web» on a screen are different, but both come from the same idea: looking through things in a relaxed way.
explain: Read the sentence around the word first. «Giraffes browse on acacia trees.» There are no shops or screens here, so browse must mean something else. Giraffes are animals, so they are feeding on the leaves and twigs.
explain: Browse can also be a noun. «Have a browse» means have a relaxed look. To check your choice, swap in your meaning: «Giraffes look through acacia trees» does not sound right, so the animal meaning is the one to choose.
fact: Browse means to look through things in a relaxed way, without searching for one particular thing.
fact: «Browse the shelves» means to look along the shelves at the books, without one special book in mind.
fact: On a computer, «browse the web» means to look at web pages on the internet. A browser is the program you use to do this.
fact: For animals, browse means to feed on the leaves and twigs of bushes and trees, as in «Giraffes browse on acacia trees». Cows are grazers: they eat grass.
fact: «Safe browsing» means visiting trusted sites online.
exercise: «Giraffes browse on acacia trees.» What does browse mean here? | To look at web pages online | To buy things in a shop | *To feed on leaves and twigs from trees | To run fast across a field
exercise: Ana says, «I'm just browsing» in a shop. What does she mean? | She is hiding from her friends | *She is looking around in a relaxed way, not searching for one special thing | She has found exactly what she wanted | She is angry with the shop
exercise: Dad says, «Have a browse while you wait.» What does a browse mean here? | A sleepy nap | A loud shout | A long race | *A relaxed look
test: In a computing lesson, what is a browser? | A tool for cutting paper | A kind of bush where giraffes live | *The program you use to look at websites
test: In science, which animal is a browser rather than a grazer? | Sheep | Cow | *Giraffe
exam: In «the giraffe browses at treetop height», what does browses mean? | Looks at web pages on the internet | Walks slowly through the shops | Hides from danger | *Feeds on leaves and twigs of trees
